SENSOR-CHECKLISTS(7)       TriadicFrameworks Manual       SENSOR-CHECKLISTS(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       sensor-checklists - laminated, at-a-glance micro-checklists for rapid
                           bridge and autonomous sensor operations

SYNOPSIS
       sensor-checklists provides:
           • ultra-compact activation sequences
           • hazard micro-checklists
           • overlay + clarity quick checks
           • harmonic/anomaly/storm/turbulence flash guides
           • emergency rollback and safe-mode triggers

DESCRIPTION
       sensor-checklists is the rapid-access, minimal-wording companion to
       sensor-ops(7). It is designed for immediate use during high-tempo
       navigation, hazard response, and constellation operations.

       These micro-checklists assume:
           • the operator is already trained
           • the sensor stack is installed and calibrated
           • time is limited and clarity is essential

       Each checklist fits on a single console tile or laminated card.

================================================================================
BASELINE STARTUP (10-SECOND CHECK)
       • overlays aligned  
       • clarity stable  
       • φ_harm jitter < 0.03  
       • spectral variance < 40%  
       • gradient polarity steady  
       • sync jitter nominal  

================================================================================
OVERLAY STACK (DRO) — QUICK CHECK
       HDO: harmonic bands separated  
       ADO: amplitude strata stable  
       SDO: no broadband spikes  
       GDO: polarity cliffs mapped  
       SFDO: sync-field coherent  

================================================================================
CLARITY STACK (CEP) — QUICK CHECK
       HPC: jitter reduced  
       RED: peaks sharp, not clipped  
       SDW: noise floor down  
       GSF: polarity smooth, cliffs visible  
       SFC: sync jitter minimized  
       ACE: terraces readable  

================================================================================
HARMONICS — FLASH GUIDE
       • φ_harm drift < 0.04  
       • overtone interference isolated  
       • lock index > 0.90  
       • chords/cascades logged  

       If φ_harm > 0.05 → HPC + reduce synthesis  

================================================================================
ANOMALY RESPONSE — 5-STEP CARD
       1. isolate band  
       2. apply clarity  
       3. reduce synthesis  
       4. reroute if needed  
       5. notify WRSADC  

================================================================================
STORM RESPONSE — 6-STEP CARD
       1. activate storm overlays  
       2. hazard nav mode  
       3. reduce synthesis depth  
       4. stabilize sync (SFC)  
       5. track front trajectory  
       6. coordinate via CCI  

================================================================================
TURBULENCE RESPONSE — 5-STEP CARD
       1. activate turbulence overlays  
       2. apply GSF  
       3. apply SDW  
       4. track flow-field  
       5. adjust fusion weights  

================================================================================
CONSTELLATION OPS — SNAPSHOT
       • sync jitter < 0.02  
       • fragmentation: none  
       • fusion layers aligned  
       • hazard maps shared  
       • lineage synchronized  

================================================================================
HAZARD THRESHOLDS — RED-LINE CARD
       φ_harm jitter > 0.05 → unsafe  
       spectral variance +50% → turbulence  
       polarity inversion → gradient hazard  
       sync jitter spike → constellation risk  
       broadband turbulence + harmonic collapse → storm precursor  

================================================================================
SAFE-MODE TRIGGER — 7-STEP CARD
       1. halt synthesis  
       2. rollback clarity  
       3. disable non-essential overlays  
       4. harmonic-only mode  
       5. recalibrate sync  
       6. re-engage synthesis slowly  
       7. log event  

================================================================================
SHUTDOWN — 6-STEP CARD
       1. disable synthesis  
       2. disable clarity  
       3. disable overlays  
       4. archive lineage  
       5. verify sync idle  
       6. power down core  

================================================================================
NOTES
       sensor-checklists is designed for rapid use under pressure. It complements
       sensor-ops(7), sensor-charter(7), and sensor-governance(7) by providing
       the shortest possible operational guidance without sacrificing safety.

